## A. Academic Year, Terms, and Calendar

Provide a shared academic calendar foundation.

Include:

- Academic year and term information.
- School holidays and working days.
- School events and important dates.
- Examination dates.
- Parent-teacher meetings.
- School activity dates.
- Staff meetings where authorized.
- Calendar views suitable for the relevant role.
- Event details, categories, date ranges, and status.

Interactions:

- View events by month, week, or list when supported by the existing UI.
- Filter by event category and date range.
- Open an event to view its details.
- Add, edit, or cancel events only for authorized roles.
- Validate event dates and required information.
- Detect obvious scheduling conflicts where practical.
- Show relevant events in authorized role dashboards.

Do not allow every role to edit the school calendar. Follow the permission registry.

## B. Announcements and Notice Board

Create one shared announcement system used by authorized role workspaces.

Include:

- Announcement title and content.
- Category and priority.
- Audience selection.
- Publication and expiry dates.
- Draft, scheduled, published, and archived states where supported.
- Author information.
- Read or acknowledgement status when relevant.
- Search and filtering.
- Announcement detail view.

Audience targeting must respect role boundaries. Examples include staff, teachers, specific classes, or authorized parent audiences.

Interactions:

- Create and edit announcements when authorized.
- Preview an announcement before publishing.
- Validate title, content, dates, and audience.
- Publish, unpublish, or archive according to permissions.
- Show relevant announcements in the appropriate dashboards.
- Allow users to mark an announcement as read when that workflow is appropriate.
- Display useful success and validation feedback.

Do not pretend that a notice has been sent through email, SMS, push notifications, or WhatsApp. The demo may show an in-app announcement and a clearly labelled simulated delivery status if needed.

