# 6. PERMISSIONS AND PRIVACY

Use the existing centralized permission registry. Do not invent a separate permission system for each shared module.

Rules:

- Deny access by default when a permission is missing or unknown.
- Check permissions when rendering protected UI and again when executing the action.
- Do not rely on hiding buttons as the only access control.
- Keep the Admin and Vice Principal permission sets distinct.
- Respect each role's existing scope.
- Restrict teachers to assigned classes, subjects, and permitted student records.
- Restrict parents to linked children and permitted family information.
- Restrict financial, HR, examination, and other sensitive information to authorized roles.
- Prevent unauthorized records from leaking through global search, notifications, directory results, exports, and related-record links.
- Do not bypass existing permissions simply to make a demonstration easier.

If the existing permission model is incomplete, improve it without removing legitimate existing capabilities. Document any permission gaps that cannot be safely resolved without clarification.

